@startuml
title Figure 1 — Verification evidence flow
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45

artifact "SRS\nrequirements.yaml\nrequirements / invariants / acceptance" as SRS
artifact "SDD\ndesign-map.yaml\ncontrolled design identities" as SDD
artifact "V&V\nverification.yaml\nstable verification obligations" as VV
component "Executable tests / checks" as Tests
component "Reusable SpecGraph\ntraceability validation" as Harness
artifact "Machine-readable\ncurrent evidence" as Evidence
artifact "Generated RTM / status views\n(disposable)" as Views
actor "Human reviewer" as Human

SRS --> VV : normative IDs
SDD --> VV : design IDs
VV --> Tests : obligations / markers
SRS --> Harness
SDD --> Harness
VV --> Harness
Tests --> Harness : executable evidence
Harness --> Evidence : deterministic graph / status
Evidence --> Views
Evidence --> Human : reproducible evidence
Views --> Human : readable projection
Human ..> VV : semantic adequacy / UX / demo validation

note bottom of Evidence
  Current pass/fail/coverage state lives in executable or generated evidence,
  never as manually copied status inside the durable V&V strategy.
end note

legend bottom
  Artifacts = controlled or generated evidence objects.
  Components = executable validation mechanisms.
  Arrows show evidence/identity flow, not work-item lifecycle.
endlegend
@enduml
